{"resourceIdentifier":"4578","resourceName":"Biochar Project-1 by WeAct","description":"This project activity is a voluntary initiative by WeAct Pty Ltd in the Sangareddy district, in the state of Telangana in India. WeAct is a carbon asset management and carbon financing entity from Australia who deals in such GHG projects globally to address the concerns of climate change and ensures long term sustainability. The project activity uses Low technology production facilities to produce Biochar from biomass wastes in the project region. The project includes mainly soil-pit methods and box-kiln method which are two common low-tech approaches that can serve as a starting point for small-scale production, experimentation, and community-level initiatives. Under the facilities, the biomass undergoes pyrolysis process. The project activity mainly targets to include “Cotton Stalk” as a single type of waste biomass used as feedstock to produce biochar and the resulting biochar to be utilized for soil application. In the absence of the project activity, the cotton wastes would have been mainly combusted without any utilization for purposes and not utilized for producing biochar for either soil or non-soil application. \r\n\r\nThe project activity is expected to generate an annual average of 22,376 tCO2e emission reductions which is estimated based on a projected generation of biochar from cotton stalks as feedstock during each harvesting season in each year. The project contributes to sustainable development by promoting various aspects including (but not limited to) environmental conservation, resource efficiency, rural development, climate change mitigation, and the transition towards a circular economy. It aligns agricultural practices with the principles of sustainable development, fostering a more resilient and equitable agricultural sector.","location":{"latitude":17.619416,"longitude":78.082307},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-08-23","endExclusive":"2023-09-23","endInclusive":"2023-09-22"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4578"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Telangana"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"WeAct Pty Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"VICTORIA, Australia"},{"type":"string","value":"vivek@weact.com.au"},{"type":"string","value":"www.weact.com.au"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification approval requested"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4578"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"21326"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0044"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4K Earth Science Private Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"12/06/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 12/04/2023 - 11/04/2030"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=95977&IDKEY=4kjalskjf098234kj28098sfkjlf098098kl32lasjdflkj909l132352283","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PROJ_DESC_PCP_4578_05JUL2023.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-08-23T14:31:10.287Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=93939&IDKEY=diquwesdfmnk0iei23nnm435oiojnc909dsflk9809adlkmlkfs129541881","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"VCS-Listing-Representation-v4.1_WeAct_signed.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-07-14T16:54:53.567Z"}]},{"code":"VCS_REGISTRATION_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Registration Documents","document